 launcher system used during WWII. It was usually mounted on a Soviet truck chassis, but this particular model was mounted on an American Studebaker US6, which was provided to the Soviet Union as part of the Lend-Lease program. The Katyusha rocket launcher system consisted of a series of rails or tubes mounted on the back of the truck. These rails held multiple unguided rockets that could be fired in quick succession, creating a devastating barrage of firepower. The rockets were typically 132 mm in diameter and had a range of around 5 to 8 kilometers. The Katyusha gained notoriety for its ability to bomb enemy positions with a large number of rockets simultaneously, causing chaos and demoralizing the opposing forces. Its distinctive sound, resembling a howling or screaming, led to its nickname \"Stalin's Organ\" among German troops.","LocalizedString":"The BM-13N, also known as Katyusha, was a Soviet rocket launcher system used during WWII. It was usually mounted on a Soviet truck chassis, but this particular model was mounted on an American Studebaker US6, which was provided to the Soviet Union as part of the Lend-Lease program. The Katyusha rocket launcher system consisted of a series of rails or tubes mounted on the back of the truck. These rails held multiple unguided rockets that could be fired in quick succession, creating a devastating barrage of firepower. The rockets were typically 132 mm in diameter and had a range of around 5 to 8 kilometers. The Katyusha gained notoriety for its ability to bomb enemy positions with a large number of rockets simultaneously, causing chaos and demoralizing the opposing forces. Its distinctive sound, resembling a howling or screaming, led to its nickname \"Stalin's Organ\" among German troops."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BrothersInArms","isInPermanentPool":true,"EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Passive","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardAttacks"],"extraHelpText